# What this file is for: nothing generated by a build, a gate or a capture is
# pushed. Two things that ARE generated stay tracked, and the reason is given
# where they are listed, because excluding them breaks the build or the gate.

# ---- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# ---- Tool and language caches ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.playwright-mcp/
*.thumbnail

# ---- Gate output ------------------------------------------------------------
# Token extraction writes here on every run; the tracked copy of the same data
# is crates/vulcan-ui/src/generated_tokens.rs.
tools/gate-fidelity/out/

# Budget measurements. One file per runner per run, uploaded as a CI artifact
# rather than committed: a measurement describes one machine at one moment.
reports/budgets/

# Written only when a comparison fails, to show what moved.
tools/gate-fidelity/reference/difference.png

# ---- Captures ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots are for human review and are regenerated by:
#   cargo run -p shell-preview -- --screenshot <path>
# They are large, change on every pixel of every UI edit, and reviewing them in
# a diff is useless. The machine's check is the fidelity comparison below.
reports/screenshots/

# The fidelity gate's working output: the capture it judged, the difference image it wrote
# and the numbers behind the verdict. All regenerated on every run. The approved baseline
# lives in tools/gate-fidelity/reference/ and IS tracked — it is the thing under review.
reports/fidelity/

# Conversion intermediates. assets/fonts/ holds the faces actually embedded, and
# tools/build-fonts.sh regenerates them from the woff2 the prototype vendors.
mockups/fonts/ttf/

# ---- Environment ------------------------------------------------------------
.env*
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ---- Deliberately NOT ignored, though generated ------------------------------
# tools/gate-fidelity/reference/shell.png and shell.json
#   The approved baseline the exact comparison judges against — a golden file,
#   not an artifact. Regenerating it in CI would compare a fresh capture to a
#   fresh capture and pass unconditionally, which is worse than having no gate.
#
# crates/vulcan-ui/src/generated_tokens.rs
#   Written by `gate-fidelity extract`, but the crate does not compile without
#   it, so a clone must build before anything can regenerate it.
#
# assets/fonts/*.ttf
#   include_bytes! into the binary, so they are build inputs. Reproducible with
#   tools/build-fonts.sh.

!docs/

# Results from a run on a Mac, and the only directory under reports/ that is
# kept. The Apple Silicon runner is the authoritative one and nobody else can
# reach that machine, so its verdicts exist nowhere but here — ignoring them
# left the project with no record of the numbers that actually decide the gate.
# `make macos-verify` clears this directory before it writes, so what is tracked
# is one run rather than an accumulation.

reports/macos/*
!reports/macos/.gitkeep
project-apex-predator.md.bak
# ---- Node / interface layer -------------------------------------------------
# Added when the Tauri + Svelte toolchain landed; the patterns above predate it.
node_modules/
dist/

# Tauri v2 writes generated schemas and platform scaffolding here on build.
src-tauri/gen/

# Copied from mockups/ by `npm run ds:sync` on every build. The signed-off
# artifact under mockups/ is the tracked source of truth; this is its build
# output, and tracking both would create two copies that can disagree.
src/lib/ds/
.e2e-profile/
# The fidelity gate's isolated profile; removed on a clean run, left behind by an aborted one.
.gate-profile/
